			"widgets_values":[
				"How the reference pictures align with the target video — <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) aligns with the 8.00-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic suspense, a continuous single shot begins on a damp street shortly after rainfall. A stable medium-long composition frames the same old metal-and-glass telephone booth shown in <Picture 1>, initially empty, with no person visible inside or nearby. Preserve the booth’s aged grey-green metal frame, fogged and rain-speckled glass, mounted black telephone, coiled metal cord, weathered notices, wet pavement, muted storefront reflections, green illuminated sign, and cool desaturated color palette. Fine droplets slide slowly down the booth windows while water drips from the roof edge. The camera initially remains still.\n\nAt approximately 1.00 seconds, the telephone inside the booth suddenly begins ringing in rapid, sharp bursts, one ring immediately following another. The camera pushes in with large amplitude at fast but controlled speed toward the booth. At approximately 1.60 seconds, the same short-haired young woman established by <Picture 1> rushes into frame from the right. She has wet chin-length black hair, a damp face, a grey suit jacket over a white collared shirt, and the same facial identity and proportions shown in the reference image. Her hurried steps are uneven and panicked.\n\nShe reaches the booth at approximately 2.60 seconds, grabs the door with her left hand, yanks it open, and rushes inside. The door rattles against its frame. She immediately seizes the black receiver with her right hand, pulls it from the cradle, and presses it firmly against her right ear. The ringing stops at the exact moment the receiver leaves the cradle. Breathless from running, she pants visibly, keeping her left hand braced against the booth’s metal doorframe for support.\n\nAt approximately 4.10 seconds, she parts her lips as if about to speak, but an unidentified caller with a low, filtered voice (S1) begins speaking through the receiver first; the words remain indistinct and unintelligible. The woman instantly freezes. Her shoulders stiffen, her breathing becomes shallow, and her eyes rapidly scan through the wet glass toward the street outside while the camera continues narrowing toward the final close composition.\n\nAt approximately 5.10 seconds, the frightened young woman with a low, breathless Mandarin voice (S2) tightens her grip on the receiver and speaks urgently under her breath: <d>[Chinese] 你到底是谁？你怎么会知道我在这里？</d> Her lips, jaw, and facial muscles synchronize precisely with every syllable. She delivers the complete line without omitting, changing, repeating, or adding words. Her brows draw tightly together, fear enters her widened eyes, and the fingers of her right hand progressively clench around the receiver. Her left hand remains spread against the booth frame as though steadying herself.\n\nAfter the final question, she falls silent and listens. Her lips stay slightly parted, her breath remains shallow, and her gaze shifts tensely toward the street beyond the booth. The camera finishes its continuous push-in. At exactly 8.00 seconds, her wet short hair, grey jacket, white collar, receiver position at her right ear, right-hand grip, left hand against the foreground doorframe, frightened expression, eye direction, telephone booth details, rain-covered glass, lighting, camera angle, depth of field, and complete final composition converge precisely to <Picture 1>.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet post-rain street ambience begins with distant traffic and steady water droplets striking metal and pavement. The telephone rings in rapid, piercing bursts until the receiver is lifted, followed by hurried wet footsteps, the booth door rattling open, the receiver leaving its cradle, the woman’s heavy breathing, and a faint filtered voice through the handset.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
